; The Tigera operator reads the MTU Calico found from /var/lib/calico, which it mounts from the host,
; and reports Calico degraded while it cannot. It runs confined, so the directory holds read-only
; content for containers; calico-node and the CNI plugin, which write there, run privileged and as
; the container runtime. Made at every boot, it is labelled before Calico writes into it, and what
; Calico writes takes its label.
(filecon "/var/lib/calico(/.*)?" any (system_u object_r container_ro_file_t ((s0) (s0))))
